4. Contact Amazon customer service separately and can only pay for shipping to the US and then make up the fee.
5. The reason for 2 points is that the customer service is good.
The first time I bought it, the product was defective, all the lights were flashing and it didn't work.
The customer requested an exchange, but the goods had not been delivered to Shanghai after three days.
They don't even answer the phone when they make the delivery.
The courier company said they only have that contact information.
Amazon cannot find a place to lodge a complaint.
I received a text message saying that there was no request for the delay, but the delivery was delayed anyway - this is what I received.
Then they said something about the transfer issue.
After all, the poor shopping experience has me questioning the effectiveness of Amazon's logistics and control systems.
I probably won't get it today.
